'''Pokémon the First Movie''' is a graphic novel published by [[VIZ Media]] in North America and [[Shogakukan]] in Japan. It is a manga-style book (called "Animation Comics" by VIZ at the time of publication, now branded as "Ani-Manga") which retells the plot of ''[[M01|Mewtwo Strikes Back]]'' and ''[[PK01|Pikachu's Vacation]]'' using screenshots from the film. [[Satoshi Tajiri]] and [[Tsunekazu Ishihara]] are credited as the authors.

In Japan, the comic was simply published as one bound volume. For the North American release, it was split up into five monthly issues, which were later rereleased in a bound volume. The first four issues tell the story of ''Mewtwo Strikes Back'', while the fifth tells the story of ''Pikachu's Vacation''.

The ''Pikachu's Vacation'' comic would later be republished in the [[All That Pikachu!]] Ani-Manga.

